--  Read by a conformance case that runs this shell from this shell, to find
--  out whether a child shell can write a great deal into a pipe. Two thousand
--  lines is a couple of hundred kilobytes: well inside what a capture will
--  hold, and far past what one pipe buffer holds -- which is the part that has
--  to work, because a program that fills the buffer waits for the parent to
--  drain it.
for Line in 1 .. 2_000 loop
   put_line ("0123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789");
end loop;

put_line ("that was all of it");
quit (0);
